+## Bounded native review: clipped-copy shortcut
+
+**Blocked: the ordinary generator does not teach a boundary behavior used by the
+existing canonical query.** The reviewed generator SHA-256 is
+`c53d61b9cea82522c91351bd5734bc84a9e48fbbab1253fadfb94b974e696084`;
+the unchanged canonical rule hash is `a9d7b3e0132a`. This packet contains no task
+review index or retained counterexample directory, and associated notes are empty.
+
+The plausible rival first discards any original color-4 source whose translated
+copy would be out of bounds, then keeps and copies the remaining sources. Both
+complete Racket programs fit all four canonical demonstrations. These fits were
+frozen before evaluating the one canonical query, where they disagree at exactly
+one cell: zero-based `(6,4)` is 4 under the authority and 0 under the rival. The
+12x13 query has vector `(6,4)`; that source would copy to `(12,8)`, outside the
+grid. The authority preserves the original 4 and clips only its copied 8.
